  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If $P=[\\begin{aligned}n & -8 \\\\ -2 & n\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-2)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ n & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 4.$",
